  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "Nxg9D92trurzIdWu+qtn1CosD+4=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:24:22.726Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The demo is a module inside racletteJS, Pacifico's own framework, dispatching typed operations from it. Building into a partner's own framework is the cheapest available seam: the maintainers control the extension point, and there is no third party to negotiate an upstream change with.\n\nThe research is careful about what that buys. Pacifico is described as small, fast and ideologically aligned \u2014 the three properties that make a first co-built reference feasible. It is explicitly not described as a route to volume, and the demo should not be read that way: its value is a working, jointly owned artefact and a public example, not a pipeline of deals.\n\nHolding those two apart matters when the work is scheduled and reviewed. Judged as a channel play, the output will be measured in deals reached and will look like a failure; judged as a reference build, it succeeds by existing and by being something a later prospect can be pointed at.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**2 \u00b7 next**\n- Pacifico Digital Explorations GmbH (DE Ottendorf-Okrilla (Dresden)) \u2014 Christian Silbermann + Michelle Fuchs, Gesch\u00e4ftsf\u00fchrer \u00b7 info@pacifico.cloud \u00b7 https://pacifico.cloud\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> racletteJS module dispatching typed operations. Small, fast, ideologically aligned partner \u2014 good for a first co-built reference, not for volume.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:24:22.726492Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:24:22.726497Z"
    }
  },
